      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:7:3:3",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ قَالَ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمِ اهْتَزَّ الْعَرْشُ إِعْظَاماً لَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Al Hassan Bin Muhammad, from Wahab Bin Hafs, from Abu ",
          "Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who says, ‘Allah<sup>azwj</sup> is the Knower’, what he does not know, the Throne shakes in Magnification for Him<sup>azwj</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from al-Hassan ibn Muhammad from Wahab ibn Hafs who has narrated the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If one says, “Allah has the knowledge”, when he does not know something, the Throne of Allah vibrates as a sign of expressing His greatness.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
